    "body": "fix on issue/794-tts-holders · PR #829 (draft, stacked on #805) · pinned by the_tts_table_is_the_recorded_one, the_tts_er20_outline_is_the_table, every_tts_profile_is_closed_and_tops_out_at_the_collar_face, a_tts_holder_tops_out_at_the_collar_the_setter_measures_from, the_tts_er20_collar_strikes_a_wall_its_nut_misses, the_picker_lists_the_tts_holders_and_names_the_collar · merges at the next cut. Machine-file default filed as #828: .mch has no holder field, and Tormach's public pages show the 770MX/1100MX are BT30, not TTS (TTS is the 770M/1100M/PCNC). Label swap claimed→in-review is for the maintainer (labels are not settable from this fork session).",
